[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[Variation "Alapin Variation, Exchange Line"]
[ECO "B22"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "isolated-pawn,blockade,d4-break"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...e6"]
[Start "nf6-main-line 2.c3"]

2... e6 3. d4 { Takes the centre. If Black takes on d4, the c-pawn recaptures. } 3... d5 ( 3... cxd4 4. cxd4 d5 5. exd5 exd5 6. Nf3 ) ( 3... Nf6 4. e5 Nd5 5. Nf3 cxd4 ( 5... Nc6 6. c4 Ndb4 7. dxc5 ) 6. cxd4 d6 7. Bc4 Be7 8. O-O ) 4. exd5 { Trades Black's centre pawn for ours and leaves Black with an isolated pawn on d5 if the c-pawn is later exchanged. The e-file opens for White's pieces. } 4... exd5 ( 4... Qxd5 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Be3 ) 5. Nf3 { Develops and guards d4. } 5... Nc6 6. Bb5 { Pins the knight on c6 to the king and adds pressure to d4's attacker, so Black has to spend time on the pawn. } 6... Bd6 7. O-O Nge7 8. dxc5 { Trades the d-pawn for the c-pawn and leaves Black with the lone d5 pawn to look after. The bishop has to move again. } 8... Bxc5 9. Nbd2 { Plan: Nb3 to chase the bishop, then a bishop on f4 or g5 and a knight on d4. The d5 pawn is a target, and the square in front of it, d4, is a perfect outpost for a White knight. } *
